title: IRS Fresh Start Program
description: Learn about the IRS Fresh Start Program and how it can help you resolve tax debt with expanded payment options and lien relief.
showBreadcrumbs: true
ctaTitle: See How Fresh Start Can Help You
ctaSubtitle: Take our free 2-minute assessment to discover which Fresh Start provisions and other relief options may apply to your situation.
faqs:
  - question: Is the Fresh Start Program a separate application?
    answer: No, Fresh Start isn't a separate program you apply for. It's a set of policy changes that affect existing relief programs. You'll apply for specific relief options (like an installment agreement or OIC) that have been made more accessible through Fresh Start provisions.
  - question: How do I get a tax lien withdrawn?
    answer: Under Fresh Start, you can request lien withdrawal if you've paid your balance in full, entered a Direct Debit installment agreement, owe $25,000 or less, and have made three consecutive payments. You'll need to submit Form 12277.
  - question: What if I owe more than $50,000?
    answer: You may still qualify for relief, but you won't be eligible for streamlined installment agreements. You'll need to provide detailed financial information and may need to consider other options like an Offer in Compromise or non-streamlined payment plan.
  - question: Will Fresh Start provisions affect my credit?
    answer: The increased lien threshold ($10,000) and lien withdrawal options can help protect your credit. Tax liens no longer appear on credit reports (as of 2018), but avoiding liens altogether is still beneficial for financial transactions.
